    "reading": "the distance does not grow with the horizon, so it is a difference in where the measurement starts and not a difference in drift. At the headline horizon it is 1.5794 bps against a fee schedule spanning 1.8 bps end to end. It is the same for every rule to within 1.3e-06 bps there, and the residue is accounted for: the two reference prices score row sets differing by 9 of 1,232,286 fills, and on those rows the quoted half-spread has nothing to cancel against. The spread across rules stays under that allowance at all three horizons and tracks the number of unshared rows in the same order"
  },
