  "where_the_positive_cells_sit": {
    "at_the_base_rung": 1,
    "at_the_discounted_rung": 67,
    "on_rungs_the_venue_charges_for": 68,
    "on_rungs_at_or_below_zero_fee": 442,
    "on_the_three_rebate_rungs": 342,
    "share_needing_zero_fee_or_a_rebate": 0.8666666666666667,
    "reading": "positivity on the trade print is mostly a subsidised-rung phenomenon, and the statement has to be made in three parts because the two-part version of it is false. One positive cell sits at the base rung an ordinary maker pays. 67 sit at the 0.4 bps rung, which is a real and attainable rung of the schedule, so saying that only one positive cell survives at a genuine venue rung would be wrong. The remaining 442 need the venue to charge nothing or to pay. Reaching the rebate rungs is not a modelling choice: money/maker_econ.py records that six maker addresses of 9,367 in this window reached the turnover share the deepest rung asks for"
  },
  "caption_this_figure_needs": "Net maker result on one common set of late-window fills, under the two reference prices the same run publishes. Left: the reported slice, both coins pooled at 10 s and the 50-fill selection rung, each band spanning the worst and best of the eleven quoting rules across the venue's six maker fee rungs. Right: how many cells of the whole grid sit above zero at each rung. ALL COUNTS ARE NOTIONAL-WEIGHTED; the equal-weighted column of the same cells gives 386 and 150 instead, so the book mid is not free of positive cells per fill. The grid holds 972 cells per reference price but not that many independent measurements: the pooled population is the union of BTC and ETH, and over the 648 cells of those two alone the counts are 338 and 0. Shading marks the rungs where the maker is charged nothing or paid; 442 of the 510 positive cells lie inside it. No uncertainty band is drawn: the artifact carries a bootstrap interval per cell and 2,376 of them cannot be shown at this size."
